comment_data.body:
Although "mark all + choose marked" is quite a common use case, the assumption during development was that it is better to be left to atomic operations. Plus creating custom action is relatively straightforward (compared to some other customizations): either emulate pressing those two keys or use a combination of [`get_picker_matches()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/12d275f4c3aeddfa12a758a69aff65090613ca34/doc/mini-pick.txt#L1226) (to get matched items) and [`get_picker_opts()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/12d275f4c3aeddfa12a758a69aff65090613ca34/doc/mini-pick.txt#L1244) (to get picker's `choose_marked` function and execute it). Here is an example of the first one:

```lua
local choose_all = function()
  local mappings = MiniPick.get_picker_opts().mappings
  vim.api.nvim_input(mappings.mark_all .. mappings.choose_marked)
end
require('mini.pick').setup({
  mappings = {
    choose_all = { char = '<C-q>', func = choose_all },
  },
})
```

